  "source": {"ace_commit":"47edade3bd3f6044b676d4eb877c4965c7eda62b","culture":"en-US","file":"Source/ACE.Server/WorldObjects/WorldObject_Networking.cs","member":"WorldObject.SerializeCreateObject / SerializeUpdateObject / SerializeGameDataOnly / SerializeUpdateModelData (through GameMessageCreateObject, GameMessageUpdateObject, GameMessageObjDescEvent)","notes":"in.object is the world object (its biota, ObjectDescriptionFlags, motion state, children, equipped items and inventory); in.dats are the synthetic portal dat files it reads, as their bytes; in.advance advances every object sequence that many times first. out: the messages built in this order: create, create with adminvision and changenodraw, update, game data only (adminvision), obj desc event; then the object's current sequences (position, movement, state, vector, teleport, server control, force position, visual desc, instance, motion).","runtime":"10.0.12","sdk":"10.0.401"}
